WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.734
-North Carolina Republican
Congressman Madison Cawthorn,

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.901
one of the most vocal proponents
of Donald Trump's

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.467
big lie about
the 2020 election,

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:11.300
lost his GOP primary last night
despite Trump's endorsement.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.801
But Trump's minions
are still moving full steam

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:15.868
ahead with their plan
for the next coup.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.234
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.934
You know, guys, politics
is a rough-and-tumble business,

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:26.634
and D.C. can be a cruel town.

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.934
Just when you feel like you're
making headway in Congress,

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:31.567
you're unceremoniously
forced out by a cruel

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.501
and unforgiving system
of cutthroats and backstabbers.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.934
And that's exactly
what happened last night

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:38.634
when one of our nation's
most committed public servants,

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:41.133
a camera-shy policy wonk
who is laser-focused

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:44.133
on serving the greater good,
lost his bid for re-election.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.200
Oh, wait. I think I read
that whole thing wrong.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:48.701
Oh, I read every word wrong.

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:50.200
It was just Madison Cawthorn.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.434
-Incumbent Madison Cawthorn has
lost the Republican nomination

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:56.534
for U.S. House District 11
seat in North Carolina.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:59.968
-State Senator Chuck Edwards
beat him with 33% of the vote.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.901
Cawthorn has officially
conceded his seat.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:05.868
-Oh, Madison, you may be gone,
but soon you'll be forgotten.

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:08.667
At least now he'll have
more time for his other job,

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:12.334
starring as the, I don't know,
bad boy villain in a CW drama?

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:13.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.000
He looks like he should be next
to a locker

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.734
threatening to tell Pacey about
Dawson's relationship with Joey.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.634
"How can you do this, Madison?
I thought we were friends."

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:26.234
"You know what they say, Dawson.
Every rose has its Cawthorn."

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.467
In this show, he plays himself.

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:35.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.033
So Cawthorn lost the GOP primary
in his district last night

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.501
after a string of scandals,

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:42.901
including accusations of insider
trading, multiple traffic stops

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:45.167
and a series
of controversial remarks like

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.567
when he called Ukraine's
president a thug.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.033
In fact, it was Republicans

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.267
who waged a relentless campaign
to take Cawthorn down.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.267
One GOP operative told
The Daily Beast,

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:57.033
"It's definitely a hit job that
I'm happy to be a party to.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.300
Most of the GOP universe

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.400
is come around to align
against this guy.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.868
You're seeing a full-court,

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:04.801
state-based establishment
pushback against him.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.667
Get this guy out.
Take him out."

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.767
I will say it's a rare treat
to watch

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:10.234
Republicans tear each
other apart

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.434
because when Republicans
decide to knife each other,

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.167
they hold nothing back.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.968
Democrats just snipe
at each other on cable news

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.300
about who's responsible
for their [bleep] poll numbers.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.033
They're like the waspy
Connecticut family

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.534
that just passive-aggressively
bickers at the dinner table

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:28.100
and then goes to bed
full of quiet resentment.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.834
Going from that
to Republican infighting,

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.934
it's like when you date someone
whose family is Italian,

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.367
you go over
to their house for dinner

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:36.567
and they're just chucking plates
of spaghetti across the room,

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.400
lunging at each other
with salad forks

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.801
because someone told Grandma
Frank Sinatra was overrated.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.400
Then 10 minutes later,
they're all hugging

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.000
and talking about
how important family is.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.934
And meanwhile, your Xanax
hasn't even kicked in.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.567
You're thinking, "I think

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.434
I maybe should have stayed with
Abigail."

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:53.767
Now, famously, the last straw
for a lot of Republicans

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:56.000
came when Cawthorn
gave an interview

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.934
claiming his GOP colleagues
did drugs

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:02.534
and invited him to orgies
or, as they were supposedly

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:05.167
billed to him,
sexual get-togethers.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:07.100
-The sexual perversion
that goes on in Washington,

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.334
I mean, being kind of
a young guy in Washington

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:12.467
where the average age
is probably 60 or 70,

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.300
and I look at all these people,
a lot of them that I, you know,

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.434
I've looked up
to through my life --

00:03:15.434 --> 00:03:16.868
I've always paid attention
to politics --

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:19.934
guys that, you know, then all of
a sudden you get invited like,

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:22.367
"Hey, we're going to have kind
of a sexual get-together

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:23.934
at one of our homes.
You should come."

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:27.601
And I'm like, "What did you just
ask me to come to?"

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:30.133
And then you realize they're
asking you to come to an orgy.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.601
Or the fact that, you know,
they're some of the people

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:34.968
that are leading on the movement
to try and remove, you know,

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:37.100
addiction in our country.
And then you watch them do it,

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.033
you know, a kilo of cocaine
right in front of you.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.534
And it's like, "Wow,
this is -- this is wild."

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.567
-Now, normally I would have
dismissed

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:48.868
that all as ridiculous,
except the GOP freaked out.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.767
Plus, there was that one time
Chuck Grassley

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.834
suspiciously gave a speech
on the Senate floor

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:56.133
with a bull full of keys
on his podium.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.901
You guys remember that?
He was all like,

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.133
"And that's why inflation is
Joe Biden's fault.

00:04:00.133 --> 00:04:03.868
Now, everybody, close your eyes
and pick a set of keys."

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:05.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.033
"And that's your special friend
till sunrise."

00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:13.167
Now, Cawthorn did get some
support from at least one corner

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:14.834
of the GOP Trump Land.

00:04:14.834 --> 00:04:16.734
Trump himself intervened
at the last minute

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.634
to reiterate his support
for Cawthorn.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.434
-Former president Donald Trump
endorsed the 26-year-old

00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:24.734
Cawthorn more than a year ago.
On the eve of the primary,

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:28.334
Trump posted on his Truth
Social platform rehashing

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.667
Cawthorn's background

00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.901
while adding, "Recently,
he made some foolish mistakes,

00:04:32.901 --> 00:04:35.000
which I don't believe
he'll make again.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.300
Let's give Madison
a second chance."

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.901
-"Let's give Madison
a second chance"

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.634
Sounds like something
you'd hear at a sorority

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:43.634
after a pledge barfs
all over the rug.

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:46.467
"Okay, I know she drank
an entire box of Franzia,

00:04:46.467 --> 00:04:47.734
but her dad knows the dean,

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:49.667
and I think we should give
Madison a second chance."

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.868
But the big takeaway
from Cawthorn's loss

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:56.000
is that when
the Republican establishment

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.200
wants to push someone out,

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.200
they are fully
capable of doing it.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.167
They could have easily done
the same thing with Trump,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.934
but they chose not to
because they decided

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.534
instead to collude with him

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:06.000
regardless
of how dangerous he is.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.200
Even now, they're continuing
to follow his lead

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.601
as he prepares for the next coup

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:11.367
and continues
spreading the big lie

00:05:11.367 --> 00:05:12.667
that the last election
was stolen.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.334
He even claims he's writing
a book about it,

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:18.634
although even he admits
it won't be good.

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:20.767
-This is the greatest -- This is
the crime of the century.

00:05:20.767 --> 00:05:22.200
I'm actually writing a book
about it called

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.534
"The Crime of the Century."

00:05:23.534 --> 00:05:25.067
I don't think you'll enjoy it.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.801
You'll be very depressed
when you read it,

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:30.501
but we want to have it down
for historic reasons.

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:33.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:36.801
-I love that despite his foray
into politics,

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:40.434
Trump remains, at his core,
a terrible salesman.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:41.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:43.901
Is this why Trump Steaks
didn't work out?

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.901
"Folks, I'm coming out
with a line of steaks.

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.868
And let me tell you right now,
you're not going to like them

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:50.834
because -- because
these steaks are tough.

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:55.033
It is like -- It's like
biting into a wallet.

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:58.300
If I'm you,
I do not go near those things."

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.567
But I do agree
that it would be historic in

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:01.868
that it would be the first book

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:06.300
ever written by someone
who has never read one.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.834
I, for real, have an easier time
picturing Donald Trump

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:13.400
doing a standing backflip
than I do him putting a bookmark

00:06:13.400 --> 00:06:16.601
between two pages
to save his place.

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:17.868
"Will you look at that?

00:06:17.868 --> 00:06:19.033
I'm late for golf.

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:22.267
Until the next time,
March sisters."

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:24.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.901
Trump tried virtually
every avenue possible

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.734
to overturn the election,
and he's still trying

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:30.100
in preparation for the next one.

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.501
He tried to get the
Supreme Court to overturn it,

00:06:32.501 --> 00:06:34.501
tried to shake down
the Georgia secretary of state,

00:06:34.501 --> 00:06:37.200
and even drafted an executive
order to seize voting machines.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.434
His plan would have used
the military,

00:06:39.434 --> 00:06:42.634
although I could just as easily
see Trump asking Rudy

00:06:42.634 --> 00:06:43.934
to seize voting machines.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.334
"Boss, I got one.

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:47.601
It's filled with fraudulent
votes for Abraham Lincoln."

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:49.434
"Rudy, that's a Coinstar."

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.200
"Oh, Rudy!"

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.234 --> 00:06:55.434
"You've done it again,
you dope!"

00:06:55.434 --> 00:07:00.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:03.100
Some in Trump's orbit
were even pushing him

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.000
to declare martial law,
like Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.334
who misspelled it
as "Marshall" law,

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:10.067
as in the name Marshall.

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.801
You know, like Marshall Mathers.

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:13.901
Oh, my God. Wait a second.
Now that I think of it,

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:16.167
the distance between the ellipse
where Trump

00:07:16.167 --> 00:07:18.334
gave his insurrection speech
and the Capitol,

00:07:18.334 --> 00:07:22.033
where the insurrection occurred
is exactly...eight miles.

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:24.567
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:07:24.567 --> 00:07:28.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:28.934 --> 00:07:30.467
It's actually only two miles.

00:07:30.467 --> 00:07:34.501
Sorry. It's just sometimes you
get so deep into a bit, you --

00:07:34.501 --> 00:07:35.567
[ Note plays ]

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:45.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.234
Are we --
Are we making the audience play

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:48.300
"Name That Tune"?

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:53.267
I can get this joke
in half of a note.

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:58.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.667 --> 00:08:01.734
Okay. Guys,
it's not going to work,

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:03.033
but we're going to do it again.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.934
[ Laughter ]

00:08:04.934 --> 00:08:06.667
Alright. So I do the eight miles
and you guys were like,

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:09.100
"Ooh, impressive."
And then I come back.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.667
You clapped. You all did.
[ Applause ]

00:08:10.667 --> 00:08:13.167
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.
And then I come back and I go,

00:08:13.167 --> 00:08:14.667
Oh, it's actually
only two miles.

00:08:14.667 --> 00:08:16.801
Oh, sorry.
Sometimes you just so -- You get

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:18.200
so deep into a bit, you --

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.868
-♪ Lose yourself ♪

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:25.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:30.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.701 --> 00:08:32.667
-Let's give Madison
another chance.

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.167 --> 00:08:43.968
And yet, curiously, whenever
they're confronted

00:08:43.968 --> 00:08:45.934
about their plans
for martial law,

00:08:45.934 --> 00:08:48.334
Trump sycophants
suddenly get very cagey.

00:08:48.334 --> 00:08:49.767
In a recent lawsuit,
for example,

00:08:49.767 --> 00:08:53.434
Greene was asked repeatedly
if she'd texted Meadows

00:08:53.434 --> 00:08:56.000
or brought up the idea
of declaring martial law

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.267
and claimed she couldn't
remember.

00:08:57.267 --> 00:08:58.601
-In those meetings,

00:08:58.601 --> 00:09:01.968
you discussed with him
your advocacy for the idea

00:09:01.968 --> 00:09:05.167
that there should be martial law
declared in the United States.

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:07.634
-No, I don't recall
ever discussing that.

00:09:07.634 --> 00:09:09.167
-Are you saying it didn't happen

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:10.467
or you're saying you don't
recall one way or the other?

00:09:10.467 --> 00:09:12.601
-I don't recall
ever discussing that.

00:09:12.601 --> 00:09:16.567
-The question was whether, prior

00:09:16.567 --> 00:09:19.534
to the inauguration
of Joe Biden,

00:09:19.534 --> 00:09:24.434
Ms. Green, whether you ever
advocated for martial law

00:09:24.434 --> 00:09:27.434
to be imposed in a conversation
with the chief of staff

00:09:27.434 --> 00:09:31.100
of the then-President of
the United States, Mr. Trump.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:34.767
-Answer the question.
-I don't recall.

00:09:34.767 --> 00:09:36.634
-Did you ever advocate
for martial law

00:09:36.634 --> 00:09:39.767
prior to the inauguration
of Mr. Biden

00:09:39.767 --> 00:09:41.934
with any member
of the White House staff

00:09:41.934 --> 00:09:44.033
that was part
of the Trump administration?

00:09:44.033 --> 00:09:45.367
-I don't recall.

00:09:45.367 --> 00:09:49.067
-I feel like I might not recall
if I advocated for, say,

00:09:49.067 --> 00:09:51.200
getting an order of ravioli
for the table to share.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:55.100
But I'd definitely remember
if I was pitching martial law.

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:56.667
Oh, wait. No, no.
Remember this one time

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:58.567
the waiter said they were
out of ravioli, and then I said,

00:09:58.567 --> 00:10:00.968
"Well, then I'm calling
in the [bleep] military!"

00:10:00.968 --> 00:10:05.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:07.868
And then there's MyPillow
CEO Mike Lindell.

00:10:07.868 --> 00:10:09.767
[ Audience groans ]
Sorry, but there is.

00:10:09.767 --> 00:10:12.868
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.868 --> 00:10:16.367
Lindell, who sells pillows
pre-loaded with nightmares,

00:10:16.367 --> 00:10:20.033
was photographed in the days
before Trump left office.

00:10:20.033 --> 00:10:23.133
Walking into the White House
with notes that said martial law

00:10:23.133 --> 00:10:25.000
on them, correctly spelled,
it should be noted.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.667
That's a real burn
on Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:28.968
when you lose the yelling bee
to the sky.

00:10:28.968 --> 00:10:31.901
But when Lindell
was confronted by a reporter,

00:10:31.901 --> 00:10:34.834
he claimed he had no idea what
the reporter was talking about.

00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:36.667
-Who gave you the papers?

00:10:36.667 --> 00:10:38.634
-Who gave me the papers?
That's none of your business.

00:10:38.634 --> 00:10:41.033
A bunch of lawyers did.
I've never read them.

00:10:41.033 --> 00:10:43.000
Hold it. I've never read them.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.801
I went in there with evidence
on January 15th.

00:10:45.801 --> 00:10:48.100
You guys are old news.
You're regurgitating old news.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:51.434
January 15th,
I went in there with four papers

00:10:51.434 --> 00:10:54.200
that shows Dominion
and the election crime

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:57.367
of the machines and China
attacking our country.

00:10:57.367 --> 00:11:01.133
Cyber attack all 50 states,
over 12 million votes,

00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:04.367
that Donald Trump won
by 82 million to 68 million,

